{{also|Appendix:Variations of "ac"}}
==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|ota|آج|tr=āc||hungry}}, from {{etyl|trk-pro|tr}} {{m|trk-pro|*āç}}, {{m|trk-pro|*ạ̄č||hunger}}.

Cognate with {{etyl|otk|-}} {{m|otk|𐰀𐰲|tr=āç||hunger, hungry}}, {{etyl|az|-}} {{m|az|ac||hungry}}, {{etyl|ba|-}} {{m|ba|ас||hungry}}, {{etyl|cv|-}} {{m|cv|выҫӑ||hungry}}, {{etyl|kk|-}} & {{etyl|tyv|-}} {{m|tyv|аш||hungry}}, {{etyl|ky|-}} {{m|ky|ач||hungry}}, {{etyl|tk|-}} {{m|tk|aç||hungry}}, {{etyl|uz|-}} {{m|uz|och||hungry}}, {{etyl|sah|-}} {{m|sah|аас||hunger}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ɑtʃ]|lang=tr}}

===Noun===
{{tr-noun|ı|lar}}

# {{label|tr|archaic}} [[hunger]]
#: {{ux|tr|'''''Acımdan''' ölüyorum.''|I am dying '''of hunger'''.|inline=1}} {{gloss|Literally '''of my hunger'''}}
# [[hungry]], [[esurient]] or [[greedy]] person or people
#: {{ux|tr|'''''Aç''' ne yemez tok ne demez.''|'''Hungry person''' eats anything, satieted person complains of everything.|inline=1}} {{gloss|A proverb}}

====Usage notes====
*The noun has two declension forms. One normal and one with /ç/→/c/.

